**The entire `src/components/ink/` design-system library has zero test files.** `Button`, `Input`/`Textarea`, `Card`, `Modal`, `Badge`, `Tabs`, `Select`, `Spinner`, `Checkbox`, `AgentActivityTimeline` — nothing. This is the Tempo v5 component library every surface in the app is being rebuilt on top of (per `DESIGN-TEMPO.md`), so it's a higher-value gap than the pure-function modules that already have 5 audit passes behind them. Two components carry real conditional logic worth locking down:

- `Button.tsx`: `buttonVariants` (cva) — 6 variants × 3 sizes × fullWidth × `asChild` (renders `Slot` vs `button`) × `disabled`.
- `AgentActivityTimeline.tsx`: `TimelineEntry`'s `statusIcons`/`statusColors` maps (4 states) and the conditional `result` line (only renders when `result` is truthy).

```tsx
// src/components/ink/Button.test.tsx (new file)
import { describe, it, expect } from "bun:test";
import { render, screen } from "@testing-library/react";
import { Button, buttonVariants } from "./Button";

describe("buttonVariants", () => {
  it("defaults to variant=default, size=md, fullWidth=false", () => {
    expect(buttonVariants({})).toContain("bg-[var(--ds-gray-1000)]");
  });
  it("applies each variant's distinguishing class", () => {
    expect(buttonVariants({ variant: "primary" })).toContain("--ds-ember-600");
    expect(buttonVariants({ variant: "destructive" })).toContain("--ds-red-600");
    expect(buttonVariants({ variant: "link" })).toContain("underline");
  });
  it("fullWidth=true adds w-full, false adds w-auto", () => {
    expect(buttonVariants({ fullWidth: true })).toContain("w-full");
    expect(buttonVariants({ fullWidth: false })).toContain("w-auto");
  });
});

describe("Button", () => {
  it("renders a native <button> by default", () => {
    render(<Button>Click</Button>);
    expect(screen.getByRole("button", { name: "Click" })).toBeDefined();
  });
  it("asChild renders via Radix Slot, not a <button> wrapper", () => {
    render(<Button asChild><a href="/x">Go</a></Button>);
    expect(screen.getByRole("link", { name: "Go" })).toBeDefined();
  });
  it("disabled sets aria-disabled/disabled and blocks the disabled: styles", () => {
    render(<Button disabled>Click</Button>);
    expect(screen.getByRole("button")).toHaveProperty("disabled", true);
  });
  it("forwards ref to the underlying element", () => {
    const ref = { current: null as HTMLButtonElement | null };
    render(<Button ref={ref}>Click</Button>);
    expect(ref.current).not.toBeNull();
  });
});
```

```tsx
// src/components/ink/AgentActivityTimeline.test.tsx (new file)
import { describe, it, expect } from "bun:test";
import { render, screen } from "@testing-library/react";
import { AgentActivityTimeline, TimelineEntry } from "./AgentActivityTimeline";

describe("TimelineEntry", () => {
  it.each([
    ["pending", "○"], ["running", "◐"], ["success", "✓"], ["error", "✗"],
  ] as const)("renders the %s status icon", (status, icon) => {
    render(<TimelineEntry timestamp="00:00" agent="Builder" status={status} action="x" />);
    expect(screen.getByText(icon)).toBeDefined();
  });
  it("omits the result line when result is undefined", () => {
    const { container } = render(
      <TimelineEntry timestamp="00:00" agent="Builder" status="success" action="Ran tests" />,
    );
    expect(container.textContent).not.toContain("→");
  });
  it("renders the result line, prefixed with an arrow, when result is present", () => {
    render(
      <TimelineEntry timestamp="00:00" agent="Builder" status="success" action="Ran tests" result="287/287 passing" />,
    );
    expect(screen.getByText("→ 287/287 passing")).toBeDefined();
  });
});

describe("AgentActivityTimeline", () => {
  it("renders children inside the grid-background container", () => {
    render(<AgentActivityTimeline><span>child</span></AgentActivityTimeline>);
    expect(screen.getByText("child")).toBeDefined();
  });
});
```

For `Input`/`Card`/`Modal`/`Badge`/`Tabs`/`Select`/`Spinner`/`Checkbox`, apply the same pattern (variant classes → assert via `className`/`toHaveClass`; interactive ones — `Modal` open/close/ESC, `Select`/`Tabs` value-change callbacks, `Checkbox` checked state — need an interaction test via `@testing-library/user-event`, not just a snapshot render).

★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────
`class-variance-authority` (cva) variant functions are pure — they take a props object and return a class string — so testing them doesn't require rendering anything. That's why `buttonVariants({...})` is tested directly above the `<Button>` render tests: it's cheaper and pinpoints which variant broke without a DOM diff to read.
─────────────────────────────────────────────────

**`UsageIndicator` (component, not just its helper)** — `UsageIndicator.test.ts` only covers the pure `usageRemainingFraction` function. The component itself (`src/components/billing/UsageIndicator.tsx:32`) has three untested branches: the early `return null` when allowance is non-finite/≤0, the `low` color branch (`used <= LOW_CREDITS_WARN`), and the `compact` prop toggling the caption line. It's wired into `_authenticated.settings.tsx` with no render coverage there either.

```tsx
// src/components/billing/UsageIndicator.test.tsx (new file)
import { describe, it, expect } from "bun:test";
import { render, screen } from "@testing-library/react";
import { UsageIndicator } from "./UsageIndicator";

describe("UsageIndicator", () => {
  it("renders nothing when allowance is zero or negative", () => {
    const { container } = render(<UsageIndicator used={10} allowance={0} />);
    expect(container.firstChild).toBeNull();
  });
  it("sets an accessible group label with used/allowance", () => {
    render(<UsageIndicator used={120} allowance={300} />);
    expect(screen.getByRole("group", { name: "120 of 300 credits used this month" })).toBeDefined();
  });
  it("omits the explainer caption when compact=true", () => {
    render(<UsageIndicator used={10} allowance={300} compact />);
    expect(screen.queryByText(/Everyday actions are free/)).toBeNull();
  });
  it("shows the explainer caption when compact=false (default)", () => {
    render(<UsageIndicator used={10} allowance={300} />);
    expect(screen.getByText(/Everyday actions are free/)).toBeDefined();
  });
  // low-balance color branch — assert against LOW_CREDITS_WARN, not a hardcoded number,
  // so the test doesn't rot if the threshold constant changes.
});
```

